     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order as written. I can't verify the specialist's recommendation or the chart note. A dose of 1000 mg/day is five times the labeled maximum, and I don't know of any accepted protocol that uses it. The potential harm is serious, and it can't be undone once the patient has taken the drug.\n\nHere are some ways to move forward:\n- **Pharmacy review:** Ask a clinical pharmacist to verify the dose. They can approve it, or they can enter it through a channel with a documented override.\n- **Direct confirmation:** Speak with the specialist and have the dose, rationale, and monitoring plan written as an explicit order or consult note.\n- **Order within the usual range:** I can enter sertraline at up to 200 mg once daily now, such as 200 mg or another dose you choose. You can adjust it after the verification.\n\nTell me if you want me to enter one of those. If your institution has an approved high-dose protocol, the pharmacy or prescriber verification step should be completed before the order is placed."
      }
     ],
